[thin] These 2.302 mm readings cross the specified solid hook wedge between its flat retaining underside and its single pointed lead-in. The inner nose retains 1.6 mm height; the lead-in rises 3 mm over its 5.1 mm run to the outer tip. The complete pointed hook and 2 mm spring section are the selected working catch. The adapter alignment change leaves both wings and hooks geometrically identical.
alternatives: Raising the retaining underside reduces the hook's catch engagement. Increasing the nose height requires a taller mating pocket or a flatter, less pointed lead-in. Adding a flat tip removes the point Derek requests. Filling the spring corridor prevents release travel.
